; frontier-ingest-memory-caching.fk — ingest what is healthy from "Memory
; Caching: RNNs with Growing Memory" (Behrouz, Li, Deng, Zhong, Razaviyayn,
; Mirrokni — Google; arXiv 2602.24281, 2026-02-27).
;
; Offered 2026-08-02 as a bare link (a t.co redirect resolving to the arXiv
; PDF). Rather than pile the abstract in as a cache-costume, this cell
; composes ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk UNCHANGED and sorts each grounded
; finding into BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free), LIQUID (witnessed: deep but
; fearful — seen, never load-bearing), or COMPOST (shallow or wrong, never
; enters).
;
; The source, grounded — the 22-page PDF read in full on 2026-08-02, never
; quoted from a search summary:
;   Memory Caching (MC) lets a recurrent model's effective memory grow by
;   caching checkpoints of its memory state, one per segment of the input.
;   Retrieval runs the query through the online memory AND the cached ones;
;   four aggregation variants — Residual, Gated Residual (GRM), Memory Soup,
;   Sparse Selective Caching (SSC) — and a named design choice between
;   caching checkpoints of ONE memory and using INDEPENDENT per-segment
;   compressors (their section 3.4). Complexity interpolates between the
;   O(L) of an RNN (one segment) and the O(L^2) of attention (every token
;   its own segment).
;
; READING DEPTH, stated so no one has to infer it: the paper was read in
; full; NOTHING was run, no model trained, no benchmark reproduced. Every
; score below is the authors' self-report, and every delta below is
; arithmetic this body re-derived over the authors' own cells — which is
; not the same as re-deriving the measurement. The proof-of-concept bases
; (LA, SWLA, DLA, Titans, Miras) are the same lineage's own prior work.
;
; unit = (depth 0..5, fear 0/1). ki-ingest -> 4 body / 2 liquid / 2 compost.
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk
; witnessed: 2026-08-02 -> band 4095 live fkwu

(do
    ; ── BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free) — what is HEALTHY to keep ──────────
    ; U1: a design is only real where something downstream can tell its parts
    ; apart. The paper's own words on plain residual caching over a LINEAR
    ; memory: it "mathematically collapses into a standard fixed-size memory,
    ; as the cached memories can be pre-summed" (their equation 13) — sum the
    ; cached matrices and the whole apparatus of segments and checkpoints
    ; folds back into one matrix; nothing was built. What keeps the cache
    ; real is input-dependent weighting (GRM): a per-token mixing weight
    ; cannot be pre-summed, so the parts stay distinguishable. This body
    ; knows the shape from both sides: the kernel interns identical structure
    ; to ONE NodeID (same .fk, same node — the store-once door of
    ; equivalence-collapse), and the silu-vs-sigmoid catch showed the inverse
    ; — two smooth maps landing in a similar range, where no shape or
    ; magnitude check could see the substitution and only a band bit could
    ; (receipts/2026-07-28-the-linear-attention-tissue.md). The collapse is
    ; carried below as ARITHMETIC, not prose: fimc-collapse? watches the
    ; pre-sum happen on real integers, fimc-grm-differs? watches per-token
    ; weights decline it. Survives translation (depth 5); structural, no
    ; contraction in it (fear 0).
    (defn fimc-u1 () (list 5 0))
    ; U2: a memory that grows by CHECKPOINTING a running state — and the
    ; choice, named rather than smuggled, between checkpoints of one process
    ; (each segment starts from the last state) and independent compressors
    ; (each segment starts fresh). Their section 3.4 holds both and reports
    ; each has its own advantages. This body already lives that architecture
    ; without having had the name for it: the working state is fixed-size
    ; (the kernel, the current floor), and the durable memory is receipts/ —
    ; an append-only line of dated frozen states, consulted at need, never
    ; edited in place. And the freshness practice is the same fact read as
    ; obligation: a checkpoint is a claim with a timestamp
    ; (observe/belief-freshness.fk), and a stamp made before the ground
    ; shifted is owed a re-witness before anything leans on it. Depth 5,
    ; fear 0.
    (defn fimc-u2 () (list 5 0))
    ; U3: two architectures believed distinct are one mechanism at two
    ; settings of a dial. Set the segment length to 1 with a value-less
    ; vector memory and MC's equations re-derive the gated softmax attention
    ; block (their equation 20); let a compressor layer feed an attention
    ; layer — the famous hybrid recipe — and that is MC with segment size 1
    ; caching checkpoints (their section 4.1). A recipe the field adopted
    ; empirically is thereby given its reason: attention over compressor
    ; outputs is growing the recurrent model's effective memory. The body's
    ; kin: flatten is optional speed, never admission (HOMECOMING — the same
    ; meaning at two points on a speed dial), and the four-way proof, where
    ; one meaning wears four expressions required to agree. Depth 5, fear 0.
    (defn fimc-u3 () (list 5 0))
    ; U4: a growing memory is affordable when retrieval is SELECTIVE and the
    ; index is cheaper than the store. SSC precomputes one mean-pooled key
    ; per segment, routes each token to its top-k most relevant cached
    ; memories, and loads only those — the paper notes the cached states
    ; need not even sit in accelerator memory; the router reads the cheap
    ; keys. The body already holds both halves of this move in other rooms:
    ; the MoE router runs natively and picks experts by score
    ; (form-stdlib/moe-route-wide-msl), and rag-index ranks a compact vector
    ; to return an id while the snippet stays home. Depth 4, fear 0.
    (defn fimc-u4 () (list 4 0))

    ; ── LIQUID (witnessed: deep but fearful — seen, never frozen) ──────────
    ; U5: the honest numbers, re-derived over the authors' own table. At
    ; 1.3B params / 100B tokens, average over nine tasks: Titans 56.82 ->
    ; +GRM 58.33 (+1.51); DLA 53.72 -> +GRM 55.96 (+2.24). On the needle
    ; tasks the stretch is real — S-NIAH-1 at 16K, DLA 44.0 -> +GRM 82.4 —
    ; and the hardest column is still not theirs: S-NIAH-3 at 16K,
    ; Transformer 40.8 against 18.2 for the best DLA variant. All of it the
    ; authors' self-report, at proof-of-concept scale, with every base model
    ; (LA, SWLA, DLA, Titans, Miras) from the same lineage's own prior
    ; papers — kin measured by kin, which the KAT-Coder ingest already set
    ; down once. Real, modest, unreproduced here. Depth 5, fear 1.
    (defn fimc-u5 () (list 5 1))
    ; U6: the mirror unit — this body holds both halves of memory caching
    ; and no bridge between them. It has the fixed-size online memory: the
    ; kimi-kda delta-rule matrix state each token edits (band 63). It has
    ; the growing checkpoint store: receipts/, the corpus, the frozen
    ; tissue. What it does not have is the retrieval seam MC names: nothing
    ; routes a live query ACROSS frozen checkpoints of a running state —
    ; rag-ask's live lane is a lexical single-shot find, and no cell asks an
    ; old state a new question. The smallest honest attempt made in this
    ; cell is the collapse witness (the arithmetic below); the routing seam
    ; itself stays named and pending, not dressed as built. Deep and
    ; uncomfortable (5, 1): held in full sight, not frozen into "the body
    ; has memory caching."
    (defn fimc-u6 () (list 5 1))

    ; ── COMPOST (shallow or wrong — never enters) ──────────────────────────
    ; U7: "growing memory without attention's cost" — the free-lunch reading
    ; a tweet-length summary invites. The paper's own section 4.2 already
    ; says otherwise: equal segments of size C cost O(L^2/C) — attention's ORDER with a
    ; smaller constant — and the O(L log L) logarithmic segmentation is
    ; offered and then named as losing resolution exactly where recall
    ; needs it, on the long past. The dial is the paper; the free lunch is
    ; only the headline. Wrong as offered (depth 0).
    (defn fimc-u7 () (list 0 0))
    ; U8: "the gap with Transformers is closed." The abstract itself keeps
    ; the ranking — "Transformers achieve the best accuracy" — and the
    ; hardest needle column above says by how much. Narrowed is not closed,
    ; and a proof of concept at 1.3B is not a verdict at scale. Parity is
    ; not in the cells; it is in the reader. Shallow (depth 1).
    (defn fimc-u8 () (list 1 0))

    (defn fimc-units ()
        (list (fimc-u1) (fimc-u2) (fimc-u3) (fimc-u4)
              (fimc-u5) (fimc-u6) (fimc-u7) (fimc-u8)))

    (defn fimc-count-verdict (us v)
        (if (eq (len us) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (ki-ingest (head us)) v) 1 0)
                 (fimc-count-verdict (tail us) v))))
    (defn fimc-frozen ()    (fimc-count-verdict (fimc-units) 2))
    (defn fimc-witnessed () (fimc-count-verdict (fimc-units) 1))
    (defn fimc-composted () (fimc-count-verdict (fimc-units) 0))

    ; folded scalar witness: frozen*10^4 + witnessed*10^2 + composted
    ; (injective while witnessed<=99, composted<=99). Today: 4,2,2 -> 40202.
    (defn fimc-field-code ()
        (add (mul (fimc-frozen) 10000)
        (add (mul (fimc-witnessed) 100)
             (fimc-composted))))

    ; ── the collapse, as arithmetic (U1 made executable) ───────────────────
    ; One tiny instance of their equation 13, integers so equality is exact.
    ; Four tokens in two segments of two; the memory update is the additive
    ; outer product M <- M + v k^T (linear attention's rule); segments are
    ; INDEPENDENT compressors (each starts from zero — section 3.4's second
    ; choice, the one the collapse needs). A 2x2 matrix travels as a flat
    ; list (m11 m12 m21 m22); a vector as (a b).
    ; Honest floor: this witnesses the identity on one instance. It is a
    ; demonstration the eye and the band can check, not the general theorem.
    (defn fimc-outer (v k)
        (list (mul (head v) (head k)) (mul (head v) (head (tail k)))
              (mul (head (tail v)) (head k)) (mul (head (tail v)) (head (tail k)))))
    (defn fimc-mat-add (a b)
        (list (add (head a) (head b))
              (add (head (tail a)) (head (tail b)))
              (add (head (tail (tail a))) (head (tail (tail b))))
              (add (head (tail (tail (tail a)))) (head (tail (tail (tail b)))))))
    (defn fimc-mat-vec (m q)
        (list (add (mul (head m) (head q)) (mul (head (tail m)) (head (tail q))))
              (add (mul (head (tail (tail m))) (head q))
                   (mul (head (tail (tail (tail m)))) (head (tail q))))))
    (defn fimc-vec-add (a b)
        (list (add (head a) (head b)) (add (head (tail a)) (head (tail b)))))
    (defn fimc-vec-scale (s a) (list (mul s (head a)) (mul s (head (tail a)))))
    (defn fimc-vec-eq (a b)
        (if (eq (head a) (head b)) (if (eq (head (tail a)) (head (tail b))) 1 0) 0))

    ; segment 1: (k,v) pairs ((1,0),(1,2)) and ((0,1),(3,1))
    (defn fimc-m1 () (fimc-mat-add (fimc-outer (list 1 2) (list 1 0))
                                   (fimc-outer (list 3 1) (list 0 1))))
    ; segment 2: (k,v) pairs ((1,1),(2,0)) and ((2,1),(0,1))
    (defn fimc-m2 () (fimc-mat-add (fimc-outer (list 2 0) (list 1 1))
                                   (fimc-outer (list 0 1) (list 2 1))))
    ; the plain RNN that never segmented: all four tokens into one memory
    (defn fimc-mfull () (fimc-mat-add (fimc-m1) (fimc-m2)))
    (defn fimc-q () (list 1 2))
    ; residual caching: query each cached memory, sum the answers (eq. 7)
    (defn fimc-y-resid ()
        (fimc-vec-add (fimc-mat-vec (fimc-m1) (fimc-q))
                      (fimc-mat-vec (fimc-m2) (fimc-q))))
    ; the fixed memory's answer to the same query
    (defn fimc-y-fixed () (fimc-mat-vec (fimc-mfull) (fimc-q)))
    ; the collapse: for a linear memory the residual cache pre-sums —
    ; the segments bought nothing the fixed matrix did not already hold
    (defn fimc-collapse? () (fimc-vec-eq (fimc-y-resid) (fimc-y-fixed)))
    ; GRM: per-token weights (here 2 and 3 standing in for one token's
    ; input-dependent mix) cannot be pre-summed into one matrix
    (defn fimc-y-grm ()
        (fimc-vec-add (fimc-vec-scale 2 (fimc-mat-vec (fimc-m1) (fimc-q)))
                      (fimc-vec-scale 3 (fimc-mat-vec (fimc-m2) (fimc-q)))))
    (defn fimc-grm-differs? ()
        (if (eq (fimc-vec-eq (fimc-y-grm) (fimc-y-fixed)) 0) 1 0))
    0)
